# ⚠️ "This trunk has no dist" WENT FALSE ON 16 Aug 2026 AND IS CORRECTED HERE
# RATHER THAN DELETED, because it is the sentence a reader would have trusted.
# The original read: "This trunk has no dist and no .env — the application that
# needed them left on 6 Aug 2026 (archive/sap-line)." The .env half still holds.
# frontend/ (G198) builds, and its two output directories are below.
# Keep this list short: a rule with nothing to match is a rule nobody notices is
# wrong. node_modules stays because a leftover tree from before the cut is still
# on disk and must never be added.

node_modules/

# The frontend build. BOTH are generated by `npm run build:frontend`, which
# `npm run check` runs before `npm test` — so frontend/dist/specimen.html, the
# page tests/design/frontend-bridge.test.ts asserts against, is REBUILT on every
# gated run rather than committed. Committing it would let the tests pass against
# an artefact that no longer matches the components that produced it, which is
# the one failure a built-page seam exists to prevent.
frontend/dist/
frontend/dist-ssr/
# The apex marketing site (G3151) — `npm run build:site`, which `build:frontend`
# runs, so it is rebuilt on every gated run for the reason above. The zip is
# `npm run package:site`'s deploy artefact and is never committed either.
frontend/site/dist/
frontend/site/dist-ssr/
frontend/site/reconcile-site.zip
.env
.env.*
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.history/
.claude/
.cursor/

# Design-tool source material. Kept on disk, out of the trunk (G33).
# Zero screens reference these — verified: grep -rho "uploads/" Mockups/rec/*.html = 0 hits.
# Move them to the design repository when one exists.
Mockups/rec/uploads/

# The CDK cloud assembly. REGENERATED by `npm run synth:infra`, which `npm run
# check` runs before `npm test` — so it is rebuilt on every gated run rather than
# committed, for the same reason frontend/dist is: a committed assembly lets a
# reader trust a template that no longer matches the app that produced it.
infra/cdk.out/
